  "seoTitle": "Indonesia Vice President Succession Updates",
  "metaDescription": "President Prabowo Subianto must submit two vice presidential candidates to the MPR by November 25, with an election scheduled for December 9, 2026.",
  "aiSummaryBullets": [
    "President Prabowo Subianto is required to submit two potential vice presidential candidates to the MPR by November 25, 2026.",
    "The MPR has rescheduled the plenary session for the election of the new vice president from December 2 to December 9, 2026.",
    "A dedicated verification team led by Habiburokhman is tasked with reviewing 22 legal requirements for the candidates before the final selection."
  ],
  "aiContextParagraph": "The vacancy in the office of the Vice President following the departure of Gibran Rakabuming Raka has prompted a formal selection process within the Indonesian government. President Prabowo Subianto holds the responsibility to propose two candidates for the position, with a submission deadline set for November 25, 2026. The MPR (People's Consultative Assembly) has established a verification team to evaluate the candidates against 22 distinct legal criteria. Various political entities, including the DPD RI, have indicated they will leave the final decision to the President. While speculation regarding potential candidates continues in public discourse, including mentions of political figures such as Yusril Ihza Mahendra and individuals from the Gerindra party, military leadership has emphasized that the armed forces remain committed to supporting the President's choice and the incoming official in their constitutional duties.",
